rachel: Heads-up I opened PR #6222 to refresh the Azure Functions quickstart for the hello-world sample. Goals: swap hardcoded key -> environment setting, show how to configure function app settings, and add a short migration note for SDK v6.

marco: Nice. Is this for the JavaScript template or C#?

rachel: I updated the Node 18 template first. We'll add C# later. Key changes: use process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY, call out Function App settings in the Azure portal, and replace streaming example with a single-response handler (Functions don't handle streaming well).

jin: Can you paste the function index.js snippet so I can sanity-check the env usage?

rachel: Pasted below:

```js
// index.js (Azure Functions - HTTP trigger)
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const apiKey = process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY
  if (!apiKey) {
    context.res = { status: 401, body: 'Missing REDWOOD_API_KEY' }
    return
  }
  const input = req.body && req.body.input ? req.body.input : ''
  const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ input })
  })
  const data = await res.json()
  context.res = { status: 200, body: data }
}
```

olivia: Small nit: Azure Function timeout defaults can be low on Consumption plan. Add a note to bump timeout on Premium or use Durable Functions for long-running jobs.

marco: Also add step-by-step for setting REDWOOD_API_KEY in Function App settings and a short CLI snippet using `az functionapp config appsettings set --name <APP> --resource-group <RG> --settings REDWOOD_API_KEY=...`. People often miss the resource group flag.

jin: Migration blurb suggestion: "SDK v5 -> v6: client constructor signature changed; if you previously used the SDK helper to inject API keys, switch to reading REDWOOD_API_KEY from environment or use Azure Key Vault (see link)." Keep it one or two lines.

rachel: Good. I'll link to the secrets+keyvault docs and include the az CLI snippet. Also adding a short troubleshooting line: if you get 401, check that app settings were deployed (sometimes deployments overwrite settings) and that the Function restarted after setting the env var.

olivia: Tiny copyedit: in the PR description "FunctionApp" -> "Function App" (two words).

